<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY — a comment ABOVE the root
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        WS2/WS5 REPOINT (2026-08-30). The `$CustomMetadata`-in-formula question this field
        was waiting on is now ANSWERED and PROVEN — see Lead.BP_Expiry__c's own comment
        block for the measurement. The literal `+ 90` becomes
        `+ $CustomMetadata.Broker_Protection_Config__mdt.Default.Protection_Window_Days__c`,
        the same record PropertyMatchingService.PROTECTION_WINDOW_DAYS,
        LeadFunnelController.BP_WINDOW_DAYS and Lead.BP_Expiry__c all resolve the window
        from, so this DISPLAY field and the ARBITRATION value can no longer drift apart.

        🔴 DEPLOY ORDER — THIS FIELD WILL NOT DEPLOY UNTIL THE CMDT *RECORD* EXISTS.
        Measured on `usman-dpeg`, 2026-08-30, against Lead.BP_Expiry__c (same shape, same
        CMDT reference) by check-only dry-run:
          • record ABSENT  -> CustomField Lead.BP_Expiry__c: "Field Default does not exist.
            Check spelling. (280:13)"  (deploy 0Afiw000000Tj09CAC, Failed)
          • record PRESENT -> Status: Succeeded, 1/1 components validated
            (deploy 0Afiw000000Tj1lCAC, proved against an existing CMDT record)
        The `Default` record is created by scripts/load-broker-protection-config.apex, NOT
        by a deploy (.forceignore excludes **/customMetadata/**). So the order for THIS
        field is identical to Lead.BP_Expiry__c's:
            1. deploy objects/Broker_Protection_Config__mdt/ (type + 8 fields)
            2. RUN scripts/load-broker-protection-config.apex
            3. only then deploy THIS field
        Deploying this field before step 2 fails with the error above, which names the
        RECORD ("Default"), not the syntax — do not read it as "$CustomMetadata is
        unsupported". It is supported at API 67.0 in this org; it was proven (on the Lead
        sibling field, since that is the one that carries the dated measurement).
    -->
    <fullName>BP_Expiry__c</fullName>
    <description>Broker protection expiry = Broker First Seen (fallback CreatedDate) + the configured protection window. The window is NOT a literal here: it resolves from Broker_Protection_Config__mdt.Default.Protection_Window_Days__c, the same record PropertyMatchingService.PROTECTION_WINDOW_DAYS, LeadFunnelController.BP_WINDOW_DAYS and Lead.BP_Expiry__c all read, so display and arbitration cannot disagree. This field will not deploy until that record exists (it is created by scripts/load-broker-protection-config.apex, not by a deploy). ⚠ TIMEZONE NOTE: DATEVALUE() on this DateTime field resolves in GMT, so a Broker_First_Seen__c instant after ~18:00 US Central can display as the next calendar day here. Same known, accepted quirk as Lead.BP_Expiry__c / Lead.Days_in_System__c - not fixed here to avoid diverging from that established Lead behavior.</description>
    <formula>DATEVALUE(IF(ISBLANK(Broker_First_Seen__c), CreatedDate, Broker_First_Seen__c)) + $CustomMetadata.Broker_Protection_Config__mdt.Default.Protection_Window_Days__c</formula>
    <formulaTreatBlanksAs>BlankAsZero</formulaTreatBlanksAs>
    <label>BP Expiry</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <type>Date</type>
</CustomField>
